ets and CIs as related to their products. Tangible/physical assets are physical items that are stocked, for example computers, monitors, and keyboards. The stages and statuses for the tangible/physical life-cycle process are visible only in hardware-related tables in Asset Management and the CMDB.","locale":"en-US","canonical_url":"https://www.servicenow.com/docs/r/servicenow-platform/common-service-data-model-csdm/csdm-lifecycle-hardware.html","release":"australia","product":"Common Service Data Model \\(CSDM\\)","classification":"common-service-data-model-csdm","topic_type":"concept","last_updated":"2026-03-12","reading_time_minutes":2,"breadcrumb":["Reference","CSDM","Configuration Management","Extend ServiceNow AI Platform capabilities"],"tags":["#servicenow-platform","#csdm","#business-services","#technical-services","#cmdb","#type-concept"]},"task_lines":[],"tasks":{},"codeblock_ranges":[]},"smart_blocks:ServiceNowOfficialDocs/servicenow-platform/common-service-data-model-csdm/csdm-lifecycle-hardware.md#---frontmatter---": {"path":null,"last_embed":{"hash":null},"embeddings":{},"text":null,"length":0,"last_read":{"hash":"hjjyss","at":1784561352073},"key":"ServiceNowOfficialDocs/servicenow-platform/common-service-data-model-csdm/csdm-lifecycle-hardware.md#---frontmatter---","lines":[1,20],"size":984,"outlinks":[],"class_name":"SmartBlock"},
